From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vm: keep bytecode packed until its code block first runs

Operands are u32s and nearly all fit in one byte, so bytecode was a
third of a compiled bundle's retained code, for functions that mostly
never run (react-dom runs 1 of 755 at load). Store it with u32-sized
operands as varints and expand it to the executable layout the first
time it executes: about 40% of the size at rest.

Upstream dropped variable-width operands (boa #4827) because decoding
them cost the interpreter 5-10%, so the interpreter never sees this
form. A packed block's executable bytes read as empty, and the dispatch
loop's existing past-the-end branch expands it, so running code pays no
extra check per instruction or per call.
